    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-generation.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "(front matter / intro)",
      "prov:value": "---\nname: theme-generation\ndescription: >\n  Turning a declared theme into CSS — `bun run cat themes:css` — and the single\n  consumer-side failure this stage exists to stop: a theme with no CSS rule\n  falls back to an opaque surface and paints over its own art. Four rounds of\n  \"still not image\" had that one cause.\n---"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-generation.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The failure: a theme with no rule paints over its own art",
      "prov:value": "So the symptom is *\"the art is not showing\"* and the cause is *\"the stylesheet\nwas not regenerated\"*. Those look nothing alike, which is why this was\nrediscovered four times rather than read once."
    }
  ]
}
